A. Twenty years ago many experts predicted that the internet would make public libraries unnecessary. Instead, visits in many towns have stayed steady, although the reasons people come have changed.

B. Fewer visitors now borrow printed books. Instead, they use free computers, attend language classes or simply find a quiet place to study. For people without fast internet at home, the library is often the only place to apply for jobs online.

C. Libraries have had to adapt. Some have replaced shelves with study rooms, and many now lend tools, musical instruments and even cooking equipment. Librarians say their main job is no longer looking after books but helping people find reliable information.', 'VALID');
